# The r2rctl bundle is a generated, byte-defined artifact: `npm run check:bundle`
# compares the committed file against a freshly compiled one for exact equality.
# Without this, git converts LF to CRLF when checking out on Windows, the bytes
# stop matching, and the reproducibility check fails on windows-latest only —
# while passing on Linux and macOS, which is how it went unnoticed.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py  text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
